.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-vpc-port-forward-add - Forward a public port of the gateway


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro vpc port-forward add  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Forward a public port of the gateway

.PP
public_ip:public_port of the gateway -> target_ip:target_port inside the VPC. The gateway must be on (409 \fBgateway_disabled\fR); one forward per protocol + public port; at most 20. \fBsource_cidrs\fR: only these public IPv4 networks may use the forward (a single IP is /32; write the network address, e.g. 198.51.100.0/24); at most 20; empty list or left out = everyone. Private, reserved and our own platform ranges are refused (422 \fBinvalid_source\fR). \fBname\fR (optional): a label of at most 64 characters.

.PP
API: POST /cloud/vpcs/{vpc_id}/port-forwards (operationId createVpcPortForward, scope cloud_write)


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--data\fP=""
	request body as JSON, @file or @- (stdin)

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	show the price quote / request without changing anything

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	idempotency key (automatic for money operations)

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	label of the forward (at most 64 characters; empty = no name). Only a label: the gateway is not touched when it changes.

.PP
\fB--protocol\fP=""
	protocol (tcp|udp)

.PP
\fB--public-port\fP=0
	public_port

.PP
\fB--set\fP=[]
	extra body field key=value (repeatable)

.PP
\fB--source-cidrs\fP=[]
	allowed source networks (public IPv4 CIDR); empty = everyone

.PP
\fB--target-ip\fP=""
	target_ip

.PP
\fB--target-port\fP=0
	target_port


